// Renovate (GitHub App, https://github.com/apps/renovate): a pull request for each new release of
// what Haul builds on, plus the "Dependency Dashboard" issue listing what is open. Their own pull
// requests: QuickJS through rquickjs (every hoster plugin and the CNL2 snippets run in it), Bun
// (image, the packageManager CI installs) and the cargo-chef of the image. Rust
// (rust:1-bookworm, dtolnay stable) and the Debian images float on purpose and are rebuilt by CI's
// weekly run.
// Everything else (the other packages, the actions, the images) comes with the shared settings of
// firsttris/workflows (renovate/default.json5): minor and patch updates once a month in one pull
// request that merges itself when CI is green, majors on request in the dashboard.
// Check with `bunx --package renovate renovate-config-validator .github/renovate.json5`.
{
  $schema: "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",
  extends: ["github>firsttris/workflows//renovate/default.json5"],
  customManagers: [
    {
      // `cargo install cargo-chef --version x.y.z` in docker/Dockerfile
      customType: "regex",
      managerFilePatterns: ["/^docker/Dockerfile$/"],
      matchStrings: ["cargo install cargo-chef --version (?<currentValue>\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+)"],
      depNameTemplate: "cargo-chef",
      datasourceTemplate: "crate",
    },
  ],
  packageRules: [
    {
      // Rust and Debian float on purpose (rust:1-bookworm, debian:bookworm-slim); a move to the
      // next Debian is a change of all three stages by hand. Haul's own image moves with its
      // releases.
      matchPackageNames: ["rust", "debian", "docker.io/tristanteu/**", "tristanteu/**"],
      enabled: false,
    },
    {
      // The plugin host: rquickjs is 0.x, so every minor can change its API
      matchManagers: ["cargo"],
      matchPackageNames: ["rquickjs"],
      enabled: true,
      groupName: "QuickJS (rquickjs)",
      sourceUrl: "https://github.com/DelSkayn/rquickjs",
      commitMessageTopic: "rquickjs",
      prBodyNotes: [
        "Every hoster plugin runs in it (`crates/haul/src/plugins/`), and the CNL2 `jk` snippet in its own runtime without host functions (docs/click-n-load.md). Before merging: read rquickjs' CHANGELOG for API changes and the QuickJS version it bundles; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo test --workspace` (the plugin host and CNL tests) must be green; the plugins are bundled for `es2020` (scripts/build-plugins.ts, still esbuild). Then run **Actions → Hoster probe → Run workflow** on this branch: its pull-request trigger does not fire for Cargo.toml.",
      ],
      schedule: ["at any time"],
      automerge: false,
      dependencyDashboardApproval: false,
    },
    {
      // Bun: the image's web stage (oven/bun) and packageManager in package.json in one PR, so CI
      // tests the Bun the image builds with. Renovate's bun manager reads "packageManager":
      // "bun@x.y.z" itself, as the npm package `bun` (no regex manager needed).
      matchPackageNames: ["docker.io/oven/bun", "oven/bun", "bun"],
      enabled: true,
      groupName: "Bun",
      sourceUrl: "https://github.com/oven-sh/bun",
      prBodyNotes: [
        "The image's `web` stage (`oven/bun:<version>` in docker/Dockerfile) and `packageManager` in package.json (CI's `bun-version-file` and the screenshots job's `npm install bun@…`) move together. Bun installs, runs the scripts, Vite and Vitest, and bundles the browser extension (`Bun.build`, extension/build.ts); the hoster plugins are still bundled by esbuild. CI's docker job builds the image when the Dockerfile changes; `bun run build` builds the plugins and the UI, `bun run build:extension` the extension.",
      ],
      schedule: ["at any time"],
      automerge: false,
      dependencyDashboardApproval: false,
    },
    {
      matchPackageNames: ["cargo-chef"],
      sourceUrl: "https://github.com/LukeMathWalker/cargo-chef",
      commitMessageTopic: "cargo-chef",
    },
  ],
}
